{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\OtpManager\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vendor-shadows-server",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "symfony/deprecation-contracts v3.6.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 32",
        "symfony/polyfill-ctype v1.33.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31",
        "symfony/polyfill-mbstring v1.33.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31",
        "symfony/polyfill-php83 v1.33.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 32",
        "symfony/translation-contracts v3.6.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 32"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "vendor/ ships 5 packages that the server ships itself in a major of Nextcloud 31 to 32. Both copies define the same classes, and the autoloader that is asked first decides which version runs.",
        "  symfony/deprecation-contracts v3.6.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 32",
        "  symfony/polyfill-ctype v1.33.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31",
        "  symfony/polyfill-mbstring v1.33.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31",
        "  symfony/polyfill-php83 v1.33.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 32",
        "  symfony/translation-contracts v3.6.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 32"
      ],
      "folds": [
        {
          "at": 4,
          "count": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ocs-unreferenced",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "POST /ocs/v2.php/apps/otpmanager/accounts/sync  ocs.otpmanager.sync.update  lib/Controller/SyncController.php:40"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 1 OCS route. OCS is there for clients outside the app, so this is no defect in itself.",
        "  POST /ocs/v2.php/apps/otpmanager/accounts/sync  ocs.otpmanager.sync.update  lib/Controller/SyncController.php:40"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "openapi-missing",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app has 21 OCS routes and no openapi.json. Clients of OCS are generated from such a specification, and nothing else tells them what these routes take and return."
      ]
    }
